        "ignore": false,
        "order": 1,
        "anno_id": 3,
        "text": "Manhattan that lies under the plan, that deceptively *untransparent* grid. It is the plan\nthat makes Manhattan safe for cruising again (it shows you where Badassin begins). As\ncomforting as it might be to have this plan to hand when venturing out of an evening, it\nhas to be suppressed for it reveals the prejudice and fear that lies beneath the surface of\nthe liberal middle-class artsy academicy intelligentsia to whom *The New Yorker* speaks\ndirectly. In more ways than one, the alienation that this cover provokes is an alienation\nfrom within.\n\n\n\n",
        "attribute": {
          "text_language": "text_english",
          "text_background": "white",
          "text_rotate": "normal"
        }
      },
